{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]I wish to the Lord I'd [C]never been [G]born
[G]Or died when I was [D]young
[G]I never would've seen your [C]sparkling [G]blue eyes
[G]Or heard your [D]lying [G]tongue
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]All the good time are [C]past and [G]gone
[G]All the good times are [D7]o'er
[G]All the good times have [C]past and [G]gone
[G]Little darling don't [D7]you weep no [G]more
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
See that eastbound passenger train
Coming around the bend
It's taken me away from this lonesome old town
To never return again
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Come back, come back my own true love
And stay a while with me
If ever I’ve had a friend in this world
You’ve been a friend to me
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_chorus}
See that lonesome turtle dove
Flying from pine to pine
He's mourning for his own true love
Why can’t I mourn for mine
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
Chorus - repeat last line to end
{end_of_verse}
